# Story 90: Sharing a Pane (50s)
# Hook: One command publishes a live pane to your workspace -- teammates watch it in real time.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-090-sharing-a-pane.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
One command publishes a live pane to your workspace -- teammates watch it in real time.

[00:03.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh with an upstream workspace configured. Sharing registers your pane on the server for remote collaborators.

[00:09.0 --> 00:16.0]
Double-Escape into rysh mode. ##share status shows whether you're connected to the upstream server.

[00:16.0 --> 00:26.0]
##share pane view publishes this pane. The ShareRegistry spawns an UpstreamShareActor that registers it on the server.

[00:26.0 --> 00:34.0]
Now anything you do here streams to subscribers. Redacted output forwards to the share's output topic continuously.

[00:34.0 --> 00:44.0]
Back in rysh mode, ##share list shows every active share in this session, each with its own share ID.

[00:44.0 --> 00:50.0]
From local pane to shared workspace in a single command. Your collaborators are now watching live.

